ial site"},"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Magdalene Tower is a landmark located at the highest point of the northern part of Drogheda, County Louth, in Ireland. All that now remains of the once important Dominican Friary is the belfry tower. Lucas de Netterville, then Archbishop of Armagh, founded the monastery in about 1224.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Magdalene Tower, Drogheda","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Magdalene_Tower_6.JPG/1280px-Magdalene_Tower_6.JPG","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Magdalene_Tower_6.JPG/500px-Magdalene_Tower_6.JPG","w":1200,"h":1600,"author":"Cianwal","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magdalene_Tower_6.JPG"}},{"id":"drogheda_beaulieu_house_and_gardens","areaId":"drogheda","name":"Beaulieu House and Gardens","category":"landmark","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":53.72805,"lng":-6.29358},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"drogheda_beaulieu_house_and_gardens","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://beaulieuhouse.ie/","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":5,"wikiPageviews":152,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["beaulieuhouseandgardens","drogheda"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Beaulieu House and Gardens is an estate in Drogheda, County Louth, Ireland. It was thought to be built in the 1660s, although later research seems to suggest it was built around 1715 incorporating elements of an earlier structure, and it includes a terraced walled garden.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Beaulieu House and Gardens","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/Beaulieu_House%2C_Co._Louth%2C_Republic_of_Ireland.jpg/1280px-Beaulieu_House%2C_Co._Louth%2C_Republic_of_Ireland.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b